    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.11.46 and relax the bundle dependencies from exact '=' pins to
'&gt;=' floors.

0.11.46 changes nothing but the pinned bundle versions: -core 0.3.320,
-json 0.1.55, -media-assets-01 0.1.33. Module code, README and LICENSE are
byte-identical to 0.11.44.

PLEASE STAGE TOGETHER with the rest of this release train, which is
submitted as separate requests:
  sr#1373544  python-comfyui-workflow-templates-json          0.1.55
  sr#1373547  python-comfyui-workflow-templates-media-assets-01 0.1.33
  sr#1373548  python-comfyui-workflow-templates-core           0.3.320
The four packages are only consistent as a set: -core's manifest names the
assets that live in -json and -media-assets-01.

On the pin change: upstream's '==' is a release-train lockfile, not an API
constraint. This meta package's only code imports five stable helpers from
-core, and the bundles are additive asset stores, so the real requirement is
one-directional -- a bundle OLDER than the manifest -core ships means a
missing asset. A floor states exactly that; '=' additionally forbids the
harmless newer direction, and that is not theoretical: while preparing this
train, bumping -core alone immediately made the 0.11.44 meta package
unresolvable in the devel project.

Verified in the build chroot with the built RPMs installed: all 528
templates and all 1235 assets resolve via iter_assets(), including the six
new ones (api_wan3_0_{t2v,i2v,r2v}, api_meshy7_{text,image}_to_model,
api_bytedance_vcube_video_enhance).
</comment>
